      "message": "[error] Line 75: 🔴 The route-change observer block captures `this` and enqueues `handleRouteChange()` asynchronously. During destruction, `removeObserver`/`CFRelease` do not synchronize with an already in-flight notification callback, so a callback can still enqueue work after teardown starts, causing use-after-free on `this`. Add a teardown guard (`std::atomic\u003cbool\u003e shuttingDown_` set before observer removal, checked in the notification block before `dispatch_async` and again in `handleRouteChange`), and ensure destructor drains/cancels pending route-change work before object memory is reclaimed.",
